# Uptime Kuma on Railway — environment variables.
# The one-click deploy needs NO variables: everything below is baked in
# or injected by Railway. Listed here for operators who want to tune.
#
# PORT — injected by Railway (the public proxy port). Uptime Kuma reads
# it directly; do not set it yourself. (Upstream default: 3001.)
# UPTIME_KUMA_PORT — upstream override for PORT if you ever run outside
# Railway. Leave unset on Railway.
# UPTIME_KUMA_HOST — bind address. Unset = all interfaces (0.0.0.0/::).
# DATA_DIR — baked to /data (the Railway volume) in the Dockerfile.
#   Holds kuma.db plus all app state. Never point it outside the volume.
# UPTIME_KUMA_DISABLE_FRAME — set to 1 to send X-Frame-Options: DENY.
# UPTIME_KUMA_SSL_KEY / UPTIME_KUMA_SSL_CERT — upstream TLS key/cert
#   paths. Leave unset on Railway (TLS terminates at the proxy).
